 "text": "Hi! How's everything today? Use I statements. Instead of saying The food here is terrible, say I don't like my chicken always cold, and it' hard to eat with my teeth still in. Wait until the end. The waiter is most interested in what everyone thinks, not just any one person's one meal. They usually just say something like, I' pass that on, and move on. Some restaurants even put a sticky note by the menu so you can leave a short message. Most people are fine with a short, honest note. Only if it' really slow or bad do most places ask for a call.",
